{"title":"2002 AIME I Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Remark\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Remark</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Jane is 25 years old. Dick is older than Jane. In <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> years, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is a positive integer, Dick's age and Jane's age will both be two-digit numbers and will have the property that Jane's age is obtained by interchanging the digits of Dick's age. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> be Dick's present age. How many ordered pairs of positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/2/d2276280d7723c5454aba6f32c7c5d4ee97a4e16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(d,n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"41\" height=\"18\" /> are possible?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let Jane's age <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> years from now be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/8/8c8b0d985d7137b67edcdd55029a03843223fe5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10a+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"58\" height=\"14\" />, and let Dick's age be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/6/91637b4521e1c07f0aa214e1070b7c2f81c10967.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10b+a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"14\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/c/08c9bd72c1d46b6e865c6a6a2bf73c62a17d4d43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10b+a&gt;10a+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"140\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/f/9dfc685c058a3923bc44dc7a591ea65066c69dea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b&gt;a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />. The possible pairs of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/b/e9bdf3e496517e8f8742f81dd774be1f93cf6e8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"18\" /> are:\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/4/14453015377b67cb285015b2c9d7cd8597a5cb43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1,2), (1,3), (2,3), (1,4), (2,4), (3,4), \\dots , (8,9)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"362\" height=\"18\" /></center>\n<p>That makes 36. But <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/8/5282e4b809ab459fc526b488610b85e58da06b6e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10a+b&gt;25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"99\" height=\"14\" />, so we subtract all the extraneous pairs: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/3/a33144f7bcd23705144df78757d5f03c9e035b54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1,2), (1,3), (2,3), (1,4), (2,4), (1,5), (2,5), (1,6), (1,7), (1,8),$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"484\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/e/a7ea22f95069bf558c1d6e41d4cab9b8a965757d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1,9)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/7/ff76feca4022bd63ac49a5d63607765ede89a9e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$36-11=\\boxed{025}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"122\" height=\"23\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Start by assuming that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/3/67340b4f3797fad0dae6c5c0c4bd13069b662d11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n &lt; 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" /> (essentially, Jane is in the 20s when their ages are 'reverses' of each other). Then we get the pairs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/f/e1f55dfbef298d9189565fe7fd2265d08e7277ce.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(61,1),(70,2),(79,3),(88,4).\\]\" width=\"224\" height=\"18\" /> Repeating this for the 30s gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/e/abe202b40f3ef28bddc6a62b026f656e84577455.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(34,9),(43,10),(52,11),(61,12),(70,13),(79,14).\\]\" width=\"384\" height=\"18\" /> From here, it's pretty clear that every decade we go up we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/4/1043c1d4198449d5f659914973d0b6c18ad7ebda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(d,n+11)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"85\" height=\"20\" /> as a pair. Since both ages must always be two-digit numbers, we can show that each decade after the 30s, we get 1 fewer option. Therefore, our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/5/6d5717a15e6000a809a437ef4b586bf0b4f83d53.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4+6+5+\\dots+2+1=4+21=\\boxed{025}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"321\" height=\"25\" />\n~Dhillonr25\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that for any \"goal age\", being <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/4/8044820d0ce0445a2b4179756f5f1173b05ea6d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d + n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"16\" />, there can only be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> ordered pair as Jane’s starting age is constant. We can work our way through Jane's possible ages when Dick can have a valid interchanged age without worrying about <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. Referring to solution one, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/f/9dfc685c058a3923bc44dc7a591ea65066c69dea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b&gt;a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Starting with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/f/1cf0953f43c76a5c79f339f9aee0fc2baac51413.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />,\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/5/795ad8e3770430e8978689a887ea97e18d350a75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = \\left\\{6, 7, 8, 9\\right\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"113\" height=\"20\" /> which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> ages for this decade.</center> \n<p><br />\nRepeating this process as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> gets larger, we get the sum \n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/6/9f6b3e55b7b08ad29960d2141c2f22e9c589eaa2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${6 + 5 + 4 + 3 + 2 + 1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"167\" height=\"15\" />.</center> \n<p><br />\nAdding our numbers, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/0/ea0a163b83e59e2adc29ed78270e6c7f4d96f195.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 + 6 + 5 + … + 2 + 1 = 4 + 21 =  \\boxed{025}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"318\" height=\"25\" />. -Exit\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Remark\">Remark</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Remark\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The 25 ordered pairs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/1/2616d1be7efa7a21163ed75e1b495cf1184dfa1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(d, n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"44\" height=\"20\" /> are:\n(34, 9)\n(34, 20)\n(34, 31)\n(34, 42)\n(34, 53)\n(34, 64)\n(43, 10)\n(43, 21)\n(43, 32)\n(43, 43)\n(43, 54)\n(52, 11)\n(52, 22)\n(52, 33)\n(52, 44)\n(61, 1)\n(61, 12)\n(61, 23)\n(61, 34)\n(70, 2)\n(70, 13)\n(70, 24)\n(79, 3)\n(79, 14)\n(88, 4)\n~Puck_0\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_I\" title=\"2002 AIME I\">2002 AIME I</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_I_Problems\" title=\"2002 AIME I Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_I_Answer_Key\" title=\"2002 AIME I Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2002\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2002 AIME I Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2002 AIME I Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2002 AIME I Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2002 AIME I Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2002 AIME I Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2002 AIME I Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2002 AIME I Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2002 AIME I Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2002 AIME I Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2002 AIME I Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2002 AIME I Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2002 AIME I Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2002 AIME I Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2002 AIME I Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2002 AIME I Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2002 AIME I Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017012105\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.034 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.055 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 239/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1786/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 108/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5687/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.707      1 -total\n 59.35%    7.542      1 Template:AIME_box\n 38.81%    4.932      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:3081:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017012105 and revision id 284867. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}